{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>If a witness of violence rises against a man.</b> Everywhere the Torah says עד ('witness') it means two, unless Scripture specifies עד אחד ('a single witness'). The sense of the verse: if two false witnesses rise against a man to testify against him — that is, to testify about him what is not so. This is the meaning of סרה: the witness is removed from that testimony — for example, two came and said to them, 'But on that day you were with us in such-and-such a place, so how did you see this in another place?'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:27.935383190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}